{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>Who has counted the dust of Jacob, etc.</b> As the Targum renders: 'the camps of the house of Jacob' — from four camps, from four standards. Another interpretation: 'the dust of Jacob' — there is no reckoning of the commandments they fulfill with dust: 'You shall not plow with an ox and a donkey' (Deuteronomy 22), 'You shall not sow mixed seeds' (Leviticus 19), the ash of the red heifer and the dust of the suspected wife and similar to them (Tanchuma)." "<b>And the number of a quarter of Israel.</b> Their quarters — the seed that issues from their relations (cf. Niddah 31)." "<b>Let my soul die the death of the upright.</b> Among them."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:12:21.594402862Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}